{
  "requirement": "Each bundled skill MUST open, before any other section, with its workflow as ordered steps. Each bundled skill, recognized by its front matter, is a site:\n\n:::{sites} skills\n```yaml\nlanguage: markdown\npaths: [assets/skills]\nrule:\n  kind: minus_metadata\nmatch:\n  - \"---\\nname: example\\n---\\n\\n# Example\\n\"\nno_match:\n  - \"# Example\\n\"\n```\n:::",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligation.** Each bundled skill MUST open, before any other section, with its workflow as ordered steps. The sites are the skills recognized by their front matter.\n\n**Site query `skills`.** Running `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow/skills` returned five whole-file nodes. They are the `SKILL.md` files of `habeas`, `habeas-requirements`, `habeas-evidence`, `habeas-bootstrap-requirements` and `habeas-refactor`, all under `assets/skills`. A text search for front-matter `name:` lines found exactly these five skill files. The other files under `assets/skills` are `references/*.md`. They have no front matter, so the query correctly leaves them out. I found no skill the query misses and no place outside the requirement's scope that it selects. The snippets fit the query. The match snippet has front matter followed by a heading. The no_match snippet is a heading with no front matter, which is the nearby code the query must not select.\n\n**Test `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_open_with_their_workflow_as_ordered_steps]`.** The test loops over `SKILLS`, which lists all five bundled skills. For each skill:\n- It takes the first `## ` heading in the raw `SKILL.md` and asserts it equals `## Workflow`. This checks that the workflow section comes before any other section.\n- It parses the section with the helper `workflow_steps`. The helper splits at `\\n## Workflow\\n` and panics if the section is missing. It collects `- [ ] N. ` steps with their continuation lines until the next `## ` heading.\n- It asserts there are at least two steps.\n- It asserts the step numbers equal `1..=n`, which checks the steps are ordered and numbered consecutively.\n\nThese assertions cover both parts of the obligation, the position of the section and its ordered steps. Every skill the site query selects is also in the test's list. I found no other obligation in the text and no unacknowledged gap.",
  "references": "bdd2c44e881310eaa176cac0bc633689971a0bf7aef8b3b2d4d14ac7fe919877",
  "inputs": [
